From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Leave out malloc_trim on uClibc-ng

uClibc-ng defines __GLIBC__ for compatibility, but provides malloc_trim
only with its malloc-standard allocator, and foot failed to build with
the others.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

--- a/terminal.c
+++ b/terminal.c
@@ -2037,7 +2037,9 @@
 
     free(term);
 
-#if defined(__GLIBC__)
+/* uClibc-ng defines __GLIBC__ too, but has malloc_trim only with one of its
+ * allocators. */
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(__UCLIBC__)
     if (!malloc_trim(0))
         LOG_WARN("failed to trim memory");
 #endif
